Greta!

Snow in Reno, the horror! Report attached (Halberd_Usage_Feb2026.pdf), and a few notes so Martin gets the story and not just the table:

- Line 1 and Line 2: 96% and 91% of seats active weekly, up from 88% and 84% in January. The Line 2 jump is the second-shift rollout in mid-February.
- Line 3: 71%, which looks low, but Line 3 ran reduced shifts for the MES prep, so the denominator is the story there, not the usage.
- Exceptions caught: 412 in February vs 380 in January; median time-to-acknowledge 11 minutes (was 18).
- Reno: 3 seats, all active, still a pilot.

One thing I'd flag for the budget conversation: Line 3 utilization will look different again in March once the MES upgrade lands, so if Martin wants a clean comparison, Q2 is the quarter to look at.

Happy to walk Martin through any of it, and looking forward to talking renewal timing whenever you're ready.

Talk soon!

